Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 09:13:36 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1193/1198] HERESY 1168: a take keeps its latents; another VAE
 decodes them again in seconds, the sound not rendered again
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Viktor, 07.10.2026: «На карте тейка три VAE. Кликнул на другой адаптер, получил обещание декодинга этим декодером, но по
ходу пошла полная синтезация трека с другим VAE, а должны лишь готовые латенты за 5-7 секунд декодироваться»; «ты как-то
сохранял готовые латенты. Вот прикрутить бы этот код к движку, и тогда будет реальная практически моментальная декОда
другим VAE». The Kit's button sent the take's replay (its music codes) with another vae: the music was not written again,
but the whole sound stage ran again before the decoder, minutes for a long song.

- The engine keeps each take's acoustic latents beside its audio: latents.f32, the layout of its own tensor dumps (debug.h:
  [ndims = 2] [T_lat] [64] as int32, then f32 time major), about 3 MB for eight minutes.
- A request with decode_from (a take of the library that kept them) runs no music and no sound stage: the latents through
  the chosen VAE alone (pipeline_decode_latents), saved as a new take of the family with the request as sent (decode_from
  never kept), its latents kept too. Asked of a take that kept none, the request is refused with that said.
- The library tells which takes kept their latents (latents: true).
- The take card's + VAE buttons: a take with latents is decoded again («in seconds»); one made before renders its sound
  again, its tip and toast saying so.

The suite: the replay carries decode_from for a take that kept its latents, and a take made before says what its button
does; the mock keeps latents for the takes it makes now (not its demo ones).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
